From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:30:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add species-by-city suitability table and model

Replaces the 27-class top_species target (about 45 cities) with one row per crop and city
(about 2,000 rows): label = crop recorded near the city, features = plain fit checks
(warm months, frost-free months, pH gap) plus city conditions and crop traits.

- dbt: mart_species_city_suitability with tests and column descriptions
- ml: train_suitability with leave-one-city-out scoring, two simple baselines
  (crop popularity, trait fit) and an honest verdict; scores saved are out-of-sample
- tests for leakage, baselines, random-label skill and metrics
- glossary entries

